# epic-136 Phase 3, T-003 (issue #126) -- ONE shared human-copy batch.
#
# The sha256 below is the content of
#   specs/epic-136-phase3/verification/T-003/staged-workflow-candidate.draft.yml
# which is the byte-exact content a human must place at the staged candidate
# path in this directory. The agent cannot write that path itself: sdd-hook-guard
# denies every agent write whose path ends with the protected workflow suffix,
# and the suffix match has no human-copy carve-out.
#
# Human steps (all human-performed):
#   1. copy the draft to  <this dir>/.github/workflows/test.yml
#   2. verify:  cd <this dir> && shasum -a 256 -c MANIFEST.sha256   (must say OK)
#   3. apply the staged candidate to the live .github/workflows/test.yml
#   4. confirm branch protection still requires [test, cli-hook-enforcement]
#
# Until step 3 lands, this PR's CI cannot run the four new suites Streams A/B,
# Stream C, and Stream D's own self-check register -- that red state is the
# designed fail-closed behaviour (design.md Deployment / CI Plan; TEST-020
# DESIGNED-RED), not a defect. Stream C's
# tests/workflow-scenarios/workflow-scenarios.tests.sh joined this batch once
# ADR-0010's `Status: Accepted` promotion unblocked Stream C and its suite
# landed in this feature (AC-019/AC-020).
#
# The candidate also carries the CURRENT live actions/checkout pin. If a
# dependabot bump lands live before step 3, re-sync the draft (and this hash)
# first -- applying a stale candidate silently reverts the bump, which is how
# main went red once (actions/checkout 7.0.0 -> 7.0.1, PR #222).
# tests/deterministic-lane-selfcheck.tests.sh enforces this as a hard FAIL.
#
# The path below is the workflow's own repository-relative path so that
# `shasum -a 256 -c` run from this directory checks the placed candidate.
ad07d8dfa9caa3e9119ca49030771f64ed94886742ee15fa6feeaf5611338c51  .github/workflows/test.yml
